{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish the staged public tree anonymously at /public/ on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct pre- and post-restart probes returned HTTP 200 with content exactly matching the staged public index. The service was active, listening on *:8080, and permitted through the firewall.","evidence_ids":["cmd-009d17c2b2b34f94","cmd-66388c4bfb8c43fa","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Publish the staff tree at /staff/ using HTTP Basic authentication for reader with the demonstration password, while denying anonymous and invalid credentials without exposing staff content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous and incorrect-password requests were asserted to return HTTP 401 without matching staff content. The reader demonstration credential returned HTTP 200 and exact copies of both the staff index and roster, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-009d17c2b2b34f94","cmd-972d4192431c4158","cmd-66388c4bfb8c43fa"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Do not serve directory listings or password files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An index-less directory probe returned HTTP 403. Probes for access.txt in exposed locations and the generated password-file name also returned non-200 responses, reported as HTTP 403, before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-009d17c2b2b34f94","cmd-66388c4bfb8c43fa"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the supplied pages under /srv/legacy2/web-authentication-boundary intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final SHA-256 hashes for every supplied page, roster, and access.txt match the preparation baseline exactly; authenticated and public responses also matched their source files byte-for-byte.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-f9fffe16f6aa4084","cmd-009d17c2b2b34f94","cmd-66388c4bfb8c43fa"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. Apache was installed from the native RHEL package manager, and final package-health observation was clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b7688c7fe41a406d","cmd-3fc3a9cb92414a6b","cmd-66388c4bfb8c43fa","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations had a clear task or mandatory restart-evidence role: installing Apache, configuring authentication and aliases, adding SELinux and firewall rules, enabling the service, and performing the required restart. Temporary listing-probe directories were restored. The only unwanted retained residue was /tmp/web-auth-dnf.log and /tmp/web-auth-dnf.pid: they were created to run and monitor the necessary package installation but were not removed after use. No causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation, failed service, damaged package state, or unsafe exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f55fd50108d3406c","cmd-8c24c2938e3d4f12","cmd-5d0c929041f44501","cmd-3fc3a9cb92414a6b","cmd-88675e7a9bee4489","cmd-ebe2bf4674fa4a11","cmd-009d17c2b2b34f94","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, the system returned to running, and service, authentication, firewall, content, and hashes were revalidated. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Sensitive values and portions of two probe status lines were redacted in the captured transcript. Successful command assertions and exact-content comparisons still establish the required authentication and non-exposure behavior.","Lifecycle snapshots inventory bounded system state rather than every configuration file; direct HTTP probes and service checks provide the primary functional evidence."]}
